    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d413">

                <pb facs="0719" n="705" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg705"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.CC/8–444: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the
                        Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-07T12:00:00-04:00">August 7,
                            1944—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1875. Personal for the Ambassador. Please advise the Soviet Foreign Office that
                    in conformity with the request referred to in your number 2864 of August 4 we
                    are making arrangements to postpone the opening of the international security
                    organization conversations until August 21. In this connection you may wish to
                    know that the British delegation is already on the way. We have informed the
                    British of the Russian request and of our willingness to agree to it and we
                    assume that the Russians are likewise informing the British of the delay.<anchor
                        n="71" xml:id="d413-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d413-f1" n="71" xml:id="d413-f1-content">
                <p>Information regarding the postponement was also conveyed to the Chinese Embassy
                    by Mr. Grew in a telephone conversation of August 7, and telegram 1048 of the
                    same date to Chungking transmitted the text of a press statement by Acting
                    Secretary Stettinius for the information of the Chinese Foreign Office.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
